    "overall_note": "Both channels share the SAME verdict here because the failure occurs at the shared EMBEDDING step (tau/m estimated once from PRE), which is upstream of and common to %DET and ENTR alike -- unlike visibility_graph's single-channel (d_B only) finding. NOT_COMPUTABLE_EMBEDDING_NOT_RESOLVED means False Nearest Neighbors (Kennel, Brown & Abarbanel 1992, R_tol=10, A_tol=2) never dropped below the 1% threshold for ANY m in 1..10 when applied to the literal Gap (b) positive-control PRE (iid Gaussian white noise) -- so %DET/ENTR could not even be computed for that PRE, let alone tested for IAAFT power. This is DISTINCT from IAAFT_LOW_POWER: no p-value could be formed at all, not that a p-value was formed but non-significant. See VALIDATION_NOTE.md for the full discussion, the fGn-H/AR1-phi resolvability boundary, and why the bootstrap fallback (tested explicitly above, not assumed) does not resolve it."
